-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  rlgl.pcpp - the rlgl unit: `import rlgl;` uses rlgl, raylib's OpenGL
  abstraction layer (rlDrawRenderBatchActive, rlEnableShader,
  rlLoadTexture, rlSetBlendMode, ...), from PaskalCPP. rlgl is compiled into
  raylib's own library, so this unit imports raylib for its include path,
  library paths and link libraries and adds only rlgl's header.
==============================================================================*/

module unit rlgl;

import
  raylib;

// The header goes to this unit's header, so every importer sees rlgl's API
cpp header;

#include "rlgl.h"

end.
